{"seq":15,"slug":"political-anthropology","title":"政治人类学","stage":"DONE","category":"anthropology","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology","rating":{"composite":3.57,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":3.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"政治人类学\">政治人类学</h1><p>如果把一群人丢在一座没有警察、没有法庭、没有国王的岛上，他们会乱成一团吗？十九世纪的欧洲人几乎本能地认为会。政治人类学这门学问之所以有趣，恰恰是因为它用一个多世纪的田野证据回答：不会，至少不必然会。秩序可以由血缘、由互惠、由对超自然报复的恐惧、由一场没人真想打赢的械斗来维系，而完全不需要一个高踞众人之上的中央权力。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 顺着四条主线层层递进，每一条都从上一条的疑问里长出来。第一条主线是「基础与理论」：先弄清政治人类学到底研究什么——不是研究政党和宪法，而是研究权力如何在任何人类群体中被分配、被争夺、被正当化；再搭起两根支柱，一根是从游群到国家的政治组织类型谱系，一根是权力、权威与正当性这组贯穿全书的概念工具。</p>\n<p>第二条主线「秩序与冲突」把镜头对准没有国家的社会，逼问那个最古典的问题：没有中央权威，秩序从何而来？答案藏在分支世系的对称制衡里，藏在大人物靠不断给予来积累影响而非命令的政治过程里，也藏在世仇与战争这种看似破坏秩序、实则维持着群体边界的暴力形式里。</p>\n<p>第三条主线「国家与权力」转向国家本身：它如何从无到有地形成，又如何借殖民统治把一种治理逻辑强加给全世界，把人口变成可计算、可管理的对象。但权力从不密不透风，于是这条主线以斯科特的「弱者的武器」收尾——日常的、隐蔽的、不上街的抵抗，提醒我们国家从来无法完全填满它声称统治的空间。</p>\n<p>第四条主线「当代」把这些古老问题带进 2026 年的现场：全球化让公民身份变得可以像资本一样流动与套利；人道主义在试图减轻苦难的同时也在治理着受苦的人口；而生物识别 ID 与算法治理正在把福柯笔下的规训重新写成代码。读完全 hub，你会发现「无国家社会如何维持秩序」与「数字时代谁在监控谁」其实是同一个问题在不同技术条件下的两次提问。</p>\n<p>建议按章节顺序阅读，但每篇文档都尽量自足，遇到别处主讲的概念会以相对链接指过去，方便你随时跳转、织成自己的知识网。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础与理论","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-core-concepts","title":"政治人类学导论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/foundations/intro-and-core-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"political-organization-typologies","title":"政治组织类型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/foundations/political-organization-typologies"},{"seq":3,"slug":"power-authority-legitimacy","title":"权力、权威与正当性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/foundations/power-authority-legitimacy"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"order-conflict","title":"秩序与冲突","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/order-conflict","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"order-in-stateless-societies","title":"无国家社会的秩序","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/order-conflict/order-in-stateless-societies"},{"seq":2,"slug":"political-process-leadership","title":"政治过程与领导","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/order-conflict/political-process-leadership"},{"seq":3,"slug":"feud-warfare-conflict","title":"世仇、战争与冲突","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/order-conflict/feud-warfare-conflict"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"state-power","title":"国家与权力","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/state-power","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"state-formation-early-states","title":"国家形成与早期国家","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/state-power/state-formation-early-states"},{"seq":2,"slug":"colonialism-postcolonial-governmentality","title":"殖民、后殖民与治理术","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/state-power/colonialism-postcolonial-governmentality"},{"seq":3,"slug":"resistance-everyday-politics","title":"抵抗与日常政治","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/state-power/resistance-everyday-politics"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"contemporary","title":"当代","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/contemporary","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"globalization-citizenship","title":"全球化与公民身份","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/contemporary/globalization-citizenship"},{"seq":2,"slug":"violence-human-rights-humanitarianism","title":"暴力、人权与人道主义","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/contemporary/violence-human-rights-humanitarianism"},{"seq":3,"slug":"digital-politics-frontiers","title":"数字时代的政治人类学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/political-anthropology/contemporary/digital-politics-frontiers"}]}]}